file: "packages/core/src/delta/merge_delta.ts"
doc:
  "Builds the union diagram a diff render draws: the target plus everything the Delta says was deleted.\n"
  "\n"
  "Vocabulary for this file is fixed in delta_overlay.spec.textproto. \"Restore\"\n"
  "always means copying a `before` snapshot into the union diagram, and is used\n"
  "for no other operation."

methods: [
  { name: "mergeDelta"
    doc:
      "Merge a Delta into its target diagram, producing a DeltaOverlay.\n"
      "\n"
      "The returned diagram is a new value. `target` is never mutated.\n"
      "\n"
      "Start from `target`: every node, edge and group key already in\n"
      "`target.graph` is copied through and recorded UNCHANGED. Then each\n"
      "entry of delta.nodeDeltas, delta.edgeDeltas and delta.groupDeltas is\n"
      "applied to its own map, by these rules:\n"
      "\n"
      "  ADDED, MODIFIED, UNCHANGED -> record that change type against the\n"
      "    key. The element itself is NOT touched: it is already in `target`,\n"
      "    which is the after state, and `after` on the entry is a copy of\n"
      "    what is already there. If the key is absent from `target`, the\n"
      "    entry is skipped entirely -- no element is created and no change\n"
      "    type is recorded.\n"
      "  DELETED -> restore `before` into the map under the entry's key and\n"
      "    record DELETED. An entry whose `before` is unset is skipped\n"
      "    entirely: there is nothing to draw.\n"
      "  CHANGE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED -> skipped entirely.\n"
      "\n"
      "Restoring a deleted element can produce a dangling reference, because\n"
      "the thing it pointed at may itself be gone. Two rules, and they differ:\n"
      "\n"
      "  A restored edge is DROPPED -- neither added to the edges map nor\n"
      "    given a change type -- when the value of its own Edge.source field\n"
      "    or its own Edge.target field names a key absent from the finished\n"
      "    union diagram's NODES map. (Edge.source and Edge.target are the\n"
      "    two endpoint fields declared in content.proto. Neither has\n"
      "    anything to do with this function's `target` parameter, which is a\n"
      "    Diagram.) An edge with a missing endpoint has nothing to route\n"
      "    between.\n"
      "  A restored node or group whose `parentGroup` names a key absent from\n"
      "    the finished union diagram's GROUPS map is KEPT, with `parentGroup`\n"
      "    set to undefined -- the optional field is left unset, not set to\n"
      "    the empty string -- so it becomes top-level. Containment is\n"
      "    decoration on an element that can stand alone, so dropping it would\n"
      "    lose a change the render exists to show.\n"
      "\n"
      "Both rules are evaluated against the FINISHED union, after every entry\n"
      "has been applied -- not against the `target` parameter. A deleted edge\n"
      "between two deleted nodes survives, because by then both endpoints are\n"
      "back.\n"
      "\n"
      "MEMBERSHIP OF A DELETED GROUP. A group's members are not listed\n"
      "anywhere; containment lives on each node's own `parentGroup`. This\n"
      "function therefore restores membership for exactly those members that\n"
      "are THEMSELVES reported DELETED, because only a restored node carries\n"
      "its `before.parentGroup` back into the union. A member reported\n"
      "MODIFIED is already in `target` at whatever parent it has NOW, and\n"
      "this function does not touch it -- so it does not rejoin its old\n"
      "group. A deleted group all of whose members survived therefore renders\n"
      "as an empty box. content.proto's comment on GroupDelta describes the\n"
      "same mechanism more loosely; where the two differ, this paragraph is\n"
      "the rule.\n"
      "\n"
      "POSTCONDITION, which DeltaOverlay relies on: when this function\n"
      "returns, every key in the returned diagram's nodes, edges and groups\n"
      "maps has an entry in the matching change-type map, and neither map\n"
      "holds a key the other lacks.\n"
      "\n"
      "This function never mentions annotations. They are not part of the\n"
      "content model -- Diagram holds a Graph of nodes, edges and groups, and\n"
      "an annotation is an AnnotationEntry in the STYLESHEET -- so there is\n"
      "nothing here to copy and nothing a Delta could have carried about one."
    inputs: [
      { name: "target", type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.Diagram" } } },
      { name: "delta",  type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.Delta" } } }
    ]
    output: { named: { symbol: "DeltaOverlay" } }
    uses: ["archeglyph.content.v1.ChangeType"]
  }
]
